# Cloudflare Pages serves static files first and only falls back to this
# file when nothing matches. Without it, a direct/hard navigation (or a
# page refresh) to a client-side route like /store/:slug — anything that
# isn't a real static asset — 404s before React Router ever loads, since
# there's no server-side route for it, only the client-side one defined in
# App.tsx. This sends every non-asset path to index.html so the SPA's own
# router can take over.
